    LLM: 'Game: Xoşkîn. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Xoşkîn is a Kurdish trick-taking card game similar to 3-player double-deck Pinochle. Played in eastern/southeastern Turkey (Northern Kurdistan). Features bidding and melds. Also known as Nezere or Pinîkêr. Name possibly derived from English 'Auction' via 'Okşin'.",
    objective: 'Win the most card points through bidding, meld declarations, and trick play; the highest total score wins the game.',
